WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.520
Welcome to our final video of this experience.

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:09.920
The M.V.P. Accelerator is over, but is there development?

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:15.520
The most powerful message you can send is that development is a continuous journey,

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:17.240
not a one-time event.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:23.080
The final part of the championship conversation is to plan the next season.

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:26.960
This solidifies the manager's multiplier effect by

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:31.520
embedding a culture of continuous growth on your team.

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:35.840
At the end of their final check-in, a coach simply asks,

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:37.520
this was a great season.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:41.400
Based on everything you've learned, what's your primary focus for

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.760
the next 90-day season?

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:48.360
This question immediately frames their accomplishments as a foundation for

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:52.240
future growth, not a final destination.

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:57.320
Your play is to end your final conversation with that exact question.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:00.480
What's the focus for your next 90 days?

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:03.200
Capture their answers in your playbook.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:08.120
This becomes a starting point for your ongoing coaching relationship.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:10.720
The ultimate challenge is this.

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:15.360
How will you take the frameworks from this program, the M.V.P. focus,

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:19.200
the 90-Day Way, the coaching for agility, and

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:23.760
embed them into everyday culture on your team?

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:25.040
What is your first move?

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:29.720
Now, go back to where we began this journey.

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:35.600
Reflect upon the one leadership behavior you wanted to strengthen for yourself.

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:37.560
How have you made progress?

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:41.640
And the one leadership behavior you wanted to improve for your team.

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:42.960
How did you see progress and

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:45.720
where did your 90-day plan support this journey?

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:51.160
As you move forward, I want you to think about this question.

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:55.640
Who will benefit from the leader you have become?

00:01:55.640 --> 00:01:59.720
Your M.V.P. isn't just a blueprint for your own success.

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:04.640
It's a blueprint for the impact you will have on the world.

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:09.640
You are leaving a legacy and making an impact that other leaders will follow.

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:14.320
You have the opportunity now to put your name on the wall of fame and

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:16.480
share your own story.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:19.840
This is how you inspire others through your journey.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:22.440
We look forward to celebrating your success.

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:26.160
Thank you for your commitment.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:29.720
You carry the weight of the workplace in many ways.

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:35.120
However, I am so proud of your commitment to your own leadership journey

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:38.120
that fuels the impact you have made on those you lead.

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:44.080
Leading from the inside out is where purpose meets performance.

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:48.040
The work you do as a coach matters more than you know.

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:53.080
It doesn't just build better employees, it builds better leaders.

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:57.200
And better leaders build a better world.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.080
Keep going.

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:00.640
You've got this.

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:02.560
Now make it happen.
